{#
  An intermediary step between "View" on document/page.njk and the
  guidance viewer itself — lets a reviewer pick a viewer layout rather
  than "View" going straight to one. See controller.js's own top comment
  for the two destinations' exact routes.

  Native govukRadios + Continue, not the earlier card-based version
  (.app-card) — the task asked for the standard GDS radio-button pattern
  ("Where do you live?") instead, so a real <form method="post"> is
  needed here now: choosing an option no longer navigates directly, it
  selects a radio, and Continue is what submits to controller.js's own
  post, which validates a selection was made and redirects to the chosen
  viewer. Validation follows the same govukErrorSummary pattern already
  established for a radios-with-Continue page in this codebase (app/
  views/v6/create-guidance/page.njk + its controller): errors.viewer =
  { text, href }, errorList: Object.values(errors), the same template
  re-rendered with the selection preserved on failure, novalidate on the
  form since the server-side check is what actually runs.

  Breadcrumbs (Home > documentTitle > current), not a Back link — GOV.UK
  guidance is not to use both on the same page, same choice every other
  breadcrumb-bearing page in this app already makes. Three levels, not
  two: the archived v6 version of this page (app/views/archive/v6/
  guidance-document-choice/page.njk) only ever had Home > documentTitle,
  which — same as the two viewer pages before this navigation redesign —
  meant nothing here linked back to the document overview page at all,
  only to the hub. The middle crumb now carries that link (per user
  feedback); the last is this page's own name, unlinked, as usual.
  Extends common/layouts/base.njk directly and hand-rolls its own grid,
  not common/layouts/content.njk — that layout's single two-thirds column
  has no room above it for a full-width breadcrumb row, the same reason
  document/page.njk and the two viewer pages do the same thing.

  Full width + context pane (see hub/page.notes.md for the navigation
  redesign this belongs to): this page sits between document/page.njk and
  the viewers, both of which already carry the pane, so it does too for
  continuity through the "View" journey, on the left, matching every
  other pane page — an .app-context-pane-row (see
  _app-context-pane.scss and document/page.njk, which uses the same
  shape), not a plain govuk-grid-row, so collapsing the pane gives the
  form's own column the width back rather than leaving it blank.

  The fieldset legend itself is this page's <h1> (isPageHeading: true,
  the same technique create-guidance/page.njk uses) rather than a
  separate heading above the radios — GOV.UK's own radios pattern always
  treats the question being asked as the page heading when the radios
  are the whole page. The explanatory paragraph becomes the fieldset's
  own hint text, rendered directly under that heading and above the
  options, which is exactly what a fieldset hint is for.
#}
{% extends "common/layouts/base.njk" %}

{% set bodyClasses = "app-full-width" %}

{% from "govuk/components/breadcrumbs/macro.njk" import govukBreadcrumbs %}
{% from "govuk/components/radios/macro.njk" import govukRadios %}
{% from "govuk/components/button/macro.njk" import govukButton %}
{% from "govuk/components/error-summary/macro.njk" import govukErrorSummary %}

{% set pageName = "Choose how you'd like to view this guidance" %}
{% if errorList and errorList.length %}{% set pageName = "Error: " + pageName %}{% endif %}

{% block content %}

<div class="govuk-grid-row">
  <div class="govuk-grid-column-full">
    {{ govukBreadcrumbs({
      classes: "govuk-!-margin-bottom-6",
      items: [
        { text: "Home", href: "/2026-09-24-context-pane/hub" },
        { text: documentTitle, href: "/2026-09-24-context-pane/document/" + id },
        { text: pageName }
      ]
    }) }}
  </div>
</div>

<div class="app-context-pane-row">

  {% include "partials/context-pane-trigger.njk" %}

  {% if not contextPane.collapsed %}
    <div class="app-context-pane-row__pane">
      {% include "partials/context-pane.njk" %}
      {% include "partials/context-pane-resize-handle.njk" %}
    </div>
  {% endif %}

  <div class="app-context-pane-row__main">

    {% if errorList and errorList.length %}
      {{ govukErrorSummary({ titleText: "There is a problem", errorList: errorList }) }}
    {% endif %}

    <form method="post" action="/2026-09-24-context-pane/document/{{ id }}/view" novalidate>

      {{ govukRadios({
        idPrefix: "guidance-viewer",
        name: "viewer",
        value: selected,
        fieldset: {
          legend: {
            text: "Choose how you'd like to view this guidance",
            isPageHeading: true,
            classes: "govuk-fieldset__legend--l"
          }
        },
        hint: {
          text: "Two ways to view this guidance are available while a new layout is being tried out. Pick either one — you can come back and try the other at any time."
        },
        errorMessage: errors.viewer,
        items: [
          {
            value: "stepper",
            text: "Stepper format",
            hint: { text: "The current guidance viewer layout." }
          },
          {
            value: "traditional",
            text: "Traditional viewer",
            hint: { text: "A new layout being tried out for viewing guidance." }
          }
        ]
      }) }}

      {{ govukButton({ text: "Continue" }) }}

    </form>

  </div>

</div>

{% endblock %}

